        .arg(Arg::new("range").long("range").value_name("RANGE").help("You can set the range of the code snippet to display for example, display the 3rd to 5th: 3:5 The syntax is similar to the range in Python or Golang, so basically you can use 3: to represent the 3rd to the end, or use :5 to represent the start to the 5th. This option is useful when you use the `from_file` option as the input, and you just want to display part of the code snippet"))
